## what this is

Every page here is a plaintext file in `blocks/`, parsed by ~450 lines of C and
shaped by ~200 lines of Lua. No database, no npm, no framework, no analytics,
no third-party requests of any kind. The absence is the point.

## who does what

C owns sockets, files, the loam parser, and escaping. Memory is one arena per
request — every allocation a request makes comes out of it, and the whole thing
is released in a single call when the response is written. There is no `free()`
in the server.

Lua owns page shapes. `lua/render.lua` is re-read on every request, so a
template edit shows up on refresh with no restart and no recompile.

## the freedom knobs

Any block header may set `skin`, `font`, `fontsrc`, `size`, `measure`, `ink`,
`paper`, `css`, and `class`. A page can ignore all of them or use every one and
look like nothing else here. [[visual-poetry]] uses six.

For anything a header line can't hold, write a stylesheet in `site/skins/` and
name it with `skin`. For anything CSS can't do, use a `:::` block and write the
HTML yourself.

## encoding media

    ffmpeg -i in.mov -c:v libsvtav1 -crf 45 -vf scale=640:-2 -an out.webm
    ffmpeg -i out.webm -frames:v 1 poster.avif
    ffmpeg -i in.wav -c:a libopus -b:a 32k out.opus

Nothing autoplays. Nothing preloads. A clip waits to be asked for.

## wasm

`make wasm`. Freestanding wasm32, no emscripten, no libc — `clang` and `wasm-ld` only. A `.c` in
`src/wasm/`, a handler in `site/js/wasm.js`, and `wasm  <name>` in a block header.

[[mandelbrot|The set]] is 1.4KB, [[garden-of-life|Life]] is 1.8KB, [[crossword|the mini]] is 2KB.

## making things disappear

`draft  yes` removes a block completely — 404, and gone from every index, tag, backlink and
transclusion. The file stays in the repo. [[library|Mounts]] are the opposite knob: things from
outside the repo, made visible.

`hidden  yes` is softer: reachable by URL, never listed.

## honesty

Every block currently in this garden is placeholder written to exercise the
system, not to say anything. Delete all of it. [[anatomy]] is the format
reference; keep that one until you have the syntax memorised.
